{"course": {"id": "s15", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Primary Mathematics — Stage 5", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "The Number System"}, {"n": 2, "t": "2D Shapes"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Numbers and Sequences"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Averages"}, {"n": 5, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (1)"}, {"n": 6, "t": "3D Shapes"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Fractions, Decimals and Percentages"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (2)"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 11, "t": "Multiplication and Division"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Data"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Ratio and Proportion"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Area and Perimeter"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Multiplying and Dividing Fractions and Decimals"}, {"n": 16, "t": "Time"}, {"n": 17, "t": "Number and the Laws of Arithmetic"}, {"n": 18, "t": "Position and Direction"}]}, "unit": {"n": 1, "stage": 15, "title": "The Number System", "strandShort": "Number", "blurb": "Place value in whole numbers and decimals with up to two decimal places, multiplying and dividing by 10 and 100, and rounding decimals.", "strand": "Number", "framework": "Cambridge Primary Mathematics (0096), Stage 5", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m5u01.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "5Np.01", "sec": "1.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Understand the value of each digit in whole numbers and decimals with one or two decimal places, and multiply and divide by 10 and 100."}, "O2": {"code": "5Np.02", "sec": "1.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Round numbers with one decimal place to the nearest whole number."}}, "sections": [{"id": "1.1", "title": "Understanding place value", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Bike race", "p": ["In a bike race, Ravi's time is **47.38 seconds**. His coach says the 3 is worth **3 tenths of a second** and the 8 is worth **8 hundredths**.", "What is each digit worth? What would the time be if it were 10 times longer? Think about it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Whole numbers", "p": ["In 5276, the 2 is worth 200."], "qq": {"id": "m5u01s1t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "What is the 7 worth in 7350?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7000, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "7000."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Tenths and hundredths", "p": ["After the decimal point come **tenths** (÷ 10) and **hundredths** (÷ 100)."], "table": {"head": ["Tens", "Ones", ".", "Tenths", "Hundredths"], "rows": [["4", "7", ".", "3", "8"]]}, "p2": ["47.38 = 40 + 7 + 0.3 + 0.08. We can also **regroup**: 47.38 = 47 + 0.38, or 46 + 1.38."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "× and ÷ by 10 and 100", "p": ["**× 10** moves each digit **one place left**; **× 100** two places. **÷ 10** moves digits one place right; ÷ 100 two places.", "47.38 × 10 = **473.8**; 47.38 ÷ 10 = 4.738 (thousandths come next!). 650 ÷ 100 = 6.5."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Value", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u01s1t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "What is the 6 worth in 3.65?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.6, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "Tenths place.", "reason": "0.6."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I work with place value?", "p": ["Step 1: Write the number in a place-value grid.", "Step 2: Read each digit's value from its column.", "Step 3: × 10 / × 100: digits move left 1 / 2 places.", "Step 4: ÷ 10 / ÷ 100: digits move right 1 / 2 places."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Decompose", "p": [], "q": "Write 26.54 as a sum.", "steps": [["20 + 6 + 0.5 + 0.04", ""]], "a": "20 + 6 + 0.5 + 0.04"}, {"k": "example", "t": "× 100", "p": [], "q": "Work out 3.7 × 100.", "steps": [["digits move 2 places left", ""], ["370", ""]], "a": "370"}, {"k": "example", "t": "÷ 10", "p": [], "q": "Work out 48 ÷ 10.", "steps": [["4.8", ""]], "a": "4.8"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Regroup", "p": [], "q": "Write 5.23 using only ones and hundredths.", "steps": [["5 ones and 23 hundredths", ""]], "a": "5 + 0.23"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Divide", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u01s1t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 72 ÷ 100.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.72, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.72."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Wrong column", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Write the value of the 4 in 2.04.", "lines": ["4 tenths = 0.4"], "bad": 0, "why": "The 4 is in the hundredths column (the 0 holds the tenths place): 0.04.", "fix": [["4 hundredths = 0.04", ""]], "id": "m5u01s1t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Forgetting the zero placeholder", "p": ["A 0 holds an empty place."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Money ($12.45) and sports times use tenths and hundredths."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Tenths, then hundredths, after the point.", "Each place is 10 times the place to its right.", "× moves digits left; ÷ moves digits right.", "Zeros hold empty places."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "1.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u01s1k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Before you read on: 47.38 × 10?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 473.8, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "1.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u01s1k02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Value of 8 in 47.38?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.08, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "1.1-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u01s1k03", "type": "num", "prompt": "650 ÷ 100?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 6.5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "1.1-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": 